# Check catalog

Every finding `validate` prints carries one of these ids. Severity is fixed per check: an error fails validation, a warning does not, and info is context. Reading findings in `SKILL.md` covers the output format and downgrading a check through `exceptions`.

## Load and schema

| Id | Severity | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| STR-001 | error | A required file or directory is missing. A stage's files are required once that stage, or a later stage that needs it upstream, is present; missing later stages are not an error. Once any stage is present, `constitution.yaml` and `reports/open-decisions.yaml` are required too. |
| SCH-000 | error | A YAML file or front matter block failed to parse, or a markdown file that needs front matter has none |
| YAML-001 | error | A YAML file or front matter block repeats a mapping key (the parser would silently keep the last value); the message names the key and both line numbers |
| SCH-001 | error | A data file violates its schema; the pointer names the field |

## Structure

| Id | Severity | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| STR-002 | error | A file in `reports/` is not one of the defined kinds: interview record (`<date>-interview-<target>.md`, the target being `prd`, `architecture`, `techspec`, `tech-spec`, `tasks`, or `realign` in any case; a record with another target gets a message naming these), `open-decisions.yaml`, audit report, constitution review, reconciliation report (`<date>-reconciliation.yaml`, or `<date>-reconciliation-<N>.yaml` for a later run the same day) |
| STR-003 | error | A spike file is not named `SPK-<ACRONYM>-<EPIC><NNN>.md`. The `OD` segment is reserved for decision-owned spikes and carries the register entry's number |
| STR-004 | error | An epic file name does not match `EPIC-<ID>-<slug>.yaml` or its id field |
| STR-005 | error | An evidence directory has no manifest; a listed file is missing; a listed bytes or sha256 differs from the file; or a file a later run compares against has no sha256, meaning every file of a `benchmark`, `stat_threshold`, or `visual_regression` manifest and any file whose `role` starts with `baseline` or `measurement` (any case). Digests are optional on other files. `produced.commit` is the head the evidence was verified at and is never checked for staleness |
| STR-006 | error / warning | A research file is not markdown (error) or has no front matter owner (warning). `research/README.md` is exempt from both |
| STR-007 | error | An active epic uses the reserved id `OD`, which names spikes owned by a register entry |

