## PRD and architecture

| Id | Severity | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| PRD-001 | error | A P0 capability appears in no flow. Runs once `architecture/` is present. |
| PRD-002 | error | A P0 job has no flow. Runs once `architecture/` is present. |
| PRD-003 | error | A capability cites an unknown job |
| PRD-004 | error | A banned synonym is also a canonical term |
| PRD-005 | warning | An entity in a Mermaid `erDiagram` block in `prd/domain-model.md` has no term in `prd/glossary.yaml`. Entities come from relationship lines (`A \|\|--o{ B : "label"`) and entity blocks (`A { ... }`); a quoted name or an `[alias]` counts. Comparison is case-insensitive, reads `_` and `-` as spaces, collapses whitespace, and lets a trailing `s` differ either way. Other diagram kinds (`stateDiagram-v2`, `flowchart`) are ignored. Skipped when either file is absent. |
| PRD-006 | warning | A constraint whose `scale` or `meter` measures time names no statistic in either. Time is the whole word millisecond(s), seconds, latency, duration, or response time, singular second after a number, or lowercase `ms` after a number or alone; a rate such as "per second" is not time. A statistic is a percentile (`p95`, `p99.9`, "95th percentile", percentile), median, mean, average, max, maximum, min, minimum, or worst case. |
| ARC-001 | error | A flow cites an unknown job, capability, or boundary |
| ARC-002 | error | A boundary or edge cites an unknown boundary |
| ARC-003 | warning | No ticket or contract references the flow. Runs once `tech-spec/` or `tasks/` is present. |

## Tech spec

| Id | Severity | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| TS-001 | error | A verification command, or a command step of a live-verification recipe, marked `exists: true` does not resolve: script missing, package script absent, or binary not on PATH. A recipe's `launch`, `doctor`, and `cleanup` are resolved, and its `drive` only when `drive_kind` is `command`. |
| TS-002 | error | A verification command or live-verification recipe marked `exists: false` has no owning active ticket. Runs once `tasks/` is present. Reconciliation refuses to archive its owner while it does not resolve (see `SKILL.md` for the remedy). |
| TS-003 | warning | A layout path does not exist and is not marked `exists: false` |
| TS-004 | error / warning | A stack pin matches no version the lockfile locks for that package (error), or the package is absent from it (warning). A lockfile may lock several versions of one package (Cargo does, as with `hashbrown` 0.12.3 and 0.16.0); a pin equal to any of them is fine. Ecosystems checked: npm, bun, cargo, pub |
| TS-005 | error / warning | A legacy sidecar's sibling `artifact` is missing (error), or a raw artifact under `tech-spec/contracts/` or `tech-spec/data-models/` has no sidecar (warning). A markdown file is a companion, not a raw artifact, only when a sidecar in the same directory names it in `companion`. One whose stem merely matches a sidecar's there (`orders.md` beside `orders.meta.yaml`, or a legacy sidecar's artifact stem) still gets the warning, which covers both cases: name a companion in `companion`; delete a legacy copy of an artifact that moved into the code. A legacy sidecar's own `artifact` is never a companion. |
| TS-007 | error | A sidecar sets both `artifact_path` and the legacy `artifact`, or neither; `artifact_path` is not repository-relative or lies inside `.constitution/`; or `artifact_path` does not exist. A missing artifact is allowed while the sidecar is `assumed` or `open` and, once `tasks/` is present, has an active creator: an active ticket that is neither `done` nor `deferred` (a deferred ticket has left the plan), named by the sidecar's optional `owner` or with `scope.in` paths covering `artifact_path` (one is the other or lies inside it). Before `tasks/` exists the creator is not checked. |
| TS-008 | warning | A sidecar uses the legacy `artifact` field, so the raw artifact lives beside it in `tech-spec/`. Move the artifact into the code, set `artifact_path`, and update `surfaces` in `constitution.yaml`. |
| TS-009 | error | A `pinned` sidecar is not settled, its artifact does not exist, and it has no active creator as TS-007 defines one. Runs once `tasks/` is present. Pinned artifacts cross epic boundaries inside a wave, so they land first; planning the artifact in an active ticket (typically the foundation epic) is the prescribed flow and is not an error. |
| TS-006 | error | An ADR's `superseded_by` does not exist, or it is superseded without one |
| TS-012 | error | Two live-verification recipes in guidelines share a name |
| TS-010 | error | A sidecar cites a flow slug or boundary id that does not exist |
| TS-011 | error / warning | An ADR's `supersedes` names an ADR that does not exist (error), or a supersession link is one-sided: A supersedes B but B's `superseded_by` is not A, or B names A in `superseded_by` but A does not list B in `supersedes` (warning) |

