| Id | Severity | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| TSK-001 | error | A ticket id is not `<ACRONYM>-<EPIC><NNN>` for its epic |
| TSK-002 | error | A ticket depends on a ticket outside its epic, or ticket dependencies form a cycle |
| TSK-003 | error | An epic depends on an unknown epic, cites an unknown capability, or epic dependencies form a cycle |
| TSK-004 | error | A ticket's in-scope path is outside its epic's declared paths |
| TSK-005 | error | A ticket's verification command is not quoted from guidelines |
| TSK-006 | error / warning | Spike ticket without a spike id or with a missing spike file, a non-spike with a spike id, a ticket carrying a decision-owned (`OD`) spike id, or an unknown closed decision. A missing spike file is an error for active and newly closing epics and a warning for previously archived ones. |
| TSK-007 | error | A ticket cites an unknown flow |
| TSK-008 | error / warning | A ticket cites an unknown constraint (error), or a benchmark or stat_threshold ticket cites none (warning) |
| TSK-009 | error | Two active epics with no dependency path between them share a scope path or a patchable tech-spec file. Patchable entries are compared by path prefix after dropping a leading `.constitution/`. |
| TSK-010 | error | A ticket, epic, or spike carries a time unit |
| TSK-012 | error | A completed epic has no closeout, or the closeout disagrees with ticket statuses or point sums |
| TSK-013 | error | An out-of-band epic has no source |
| TSK-014 | error | A ticket's acceptance includes `live_probe` (as the mode or a supplementary mode) but names no `recipe`, names a `recipe` without `live_probe`, or names a recipe guidelines does not declare under `live_verification` |
| TSK-015 | warning | An active epic has no `estimated_diff_lines`, or a completed epic whose `estimate_source` is `planned` (or absent) has an estimate exactly equal to its measured diff, which suggests it was filled from actuals; `migrate --repair-estimates` marks those `backfilled`. |
| TSK-016 | error | An active or newly closing epic's closeout names a `settled[].record` that reconcile could not resolve (missing file, a list file without that record id, a non-list file that is not a certainty-bearing record such as `tech-spec/guidelines.md`, or a path that is absolute, has a `..` segment, or resolves outside `.constitution/`, which reconcile refuses to write), or a `spec_patches[].path` that does not exist. Reconciliation keeps this check before archival. |
| TSK-017 | warning | An active epic's `tech_spec_patchable` names a raw artifact under `tech-spec/` (a markdown companion, as TS-005 defines it, is not one). Name its sidecar instead; once the artifact lives in the code, its path belongs in `scope.paths`. |
| TSK-018 | error / warning | A `done` ticket owns evidence (a manifest whose `owner` is the ticket or whose `covers` lists it, or one in `evidence/<ticket>/` or `evidence/<ticket>-live/`) that records `result: fail` or `not_met`, or records `owed` while the epic has a closeout whose `follow_ups` has no entry naming the ticket id. Error in active and newly closing epics, warning in previously archived ones. Only ticket owners are checked, not evidence owned by a spike or constraint |
| TSK-019 | error | In an active or newly closing epic with a closeout, a `done` ticket accepted by `live_probe` (as the mode or a supplementary mode) owns no evidence manifest whose `mode` is `live_probe`, or its live_probe manifests record no `result`. Epics without a closeout are still in flight and previously archived epics are exempt |
| TSK-020 | error / warning | Invalid obligation ownership or resolution: unknown or conflicting source records, duplicate ticket records, unresolved ownership forks, replacement cycles, conflicting outcomes for one reference, or missing explicit evidence (retirement also needs a reason). Warnings mark repository evidence preserved by an artifact at the recorded full git SHA, and previously archived claims without available proof. Deferred obligations in `SKILL.md` defines source references, precedence, and what keeps an obligation outstanding. |
| INFO-EST | info | Share of open tickets estimated at the ceiling |
| INFO-CAL | info | `calibration: actual/estimate = R over N completed epics; M excluded`. R is total measured diff lines over total estimated diff lines, counting only completed epics with actuals and a planned estimate above zero; migrated and backfilled estimates, and planned ones that equal actuals exactly, are excluded. Runs once `tasks/` has a completed epic. |
| INFO-PLAN | info | Active epic count, out-of-band count, and open points. Runs once `tasks/` is present. |
| INFO-SHAPE | info | Which stage directories are present |

